Description: Gate PWM writes on a board allowlist and the DMI system vendor
 Upstream enabled writes for every validated profile and, with
 experimental_write=1, for every experimental profile and for force-loaded
 unknown systems (c:585-587). The package sets experimental_write=1, so
 force=1 on any other machine opened PMC2 writes to an unknown EC (A2,
 critical). The DMI table matches product and board name only, no vendor
 (A1, critical by impact). The EC command set and the channel map are
 board firmware, not a property of the IT5571 chip, so the same chip on
 another board is no reason to write.
 .
 Writes are now enabled only if DMI sys_vendor is exactly "Micro Computer
 (HK) Tech Limited" (measured on the reference N5 Pro, befunde/raw/
 01-baseline-20260914-160216.txt:10) AND either the profile is validated
 upstream (N5/F8NAA) or experimental_write=1 and the profile is in the
 downstream write allowlist, which holds only N5 PRO/F8NAA. A force-loaded
 unknown system is always read-only, experimental_write is ignored there.
 N5 Air/F8NAB is read-only. The probe logs why writes are off.
 .
 The N5 PRO/F8NAA DMI entry additionally matches DMI_SYS_VENDOR exactly
 (the measured value), so an N5 PRO/F8NAA board from another vendor does
 not bind without force=1, and then only read-only. The N5 and N5 Air
 entries stay as upstream, without vendor, because their vendor string is
 not measured: they still bind read-only on a vendor mismatch, and sensor
 reads still send EC read commands there. Consequence for the
 upstream-validated N5: if its sys_vendor differs from the N5 Pro value,
 it binds read-only (safe direction, documented in the README).
 .
 Resolves A1 (target board: vendor in the match and in the write gate;
 N5/N5 Air: vendor in the write gate only, residual documented), A2, A11
 (force behaves as documented), A13 (behaviour now matches the text from
 0001), the A3 note (validated N5 writes without opt-in only with the
 vendor match). Mitigates A9: the module alias is still a substring glob
 and modules-load.d still loads it everywhere the package is installed,
 but a wrong binding can no longer write.
 .
 Tested: build/static analysis as 0001; modinfo alias of the N5 PRO entry
 contains svnMicroComputer(HK)TechLimited. Not tested on hardware: binding
 and dmesg on the N5 Pro with experimental_write=1 (writes on) and =0
 (read-only, pwm* hidden).
